# ---- Environment & secrets ----
# Root .env used to be DELIBERATELY tracked in this repo (see docs/12_SESSION_CONTEXT.md
# for that original exception and why it was made). That policy was reversed on
# 2026-09-06 — .env is untracked going forward (git rm --cached) and every real
# value now lives in .env.local instead. .env.example remains the checked-in
# template. Values committed under the old policy (JWT_SECRET, POSTGRES_PASSWORD)
# are already in git history and were not rotated by this change alone.
.env
backend/.env
# API keys for image generation etc. Never committed — the key lives here
# instead of .env precisely so it cannot ride along with the tracked .env.
.secrets/
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.key
*.pem

# ---- Python / backend ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# ---- Node / frontend ----
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---- Runtime data ----
logs/
*.log
.trash/

# ---- IDE / OS ----
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- AI assistant local state ----
# Skills are installed per-developer from upstream, never vendored here: they
# are third-party content we don't own the right to redistribute, and at least
# one (tailwind-4-docs) ships a snapshot its own author marks source-available
# but not open-source. Install instructions live in docs/11_AI_TOOLING.md.
.claude/

# ---- Merge artefacts ----
# A stray .orig/.rej committed during a conflict is how a half-resolved merge
# reaches main. See docs/10_LESSONS.md §1.
*.orig
*.rej

# ---- QA run artifacts ----
# Generated by qa/run_account_module_tests.py on every run. Timestamped
# reports pile up fast and can carry single lines 100k+ chars long, which
# hangs VS Code's diff viewer when staged. Regenerable, not source.
qa/reports/

# ---- Working docs ----
# `docs/` and `ai_guidelines/` are deliberately TRACKED, not ignored. The
# virtual round ignored them, and two committed READMEs then linked to files
# that did not exist in a fresh clone (docs/10_LESSONS.md §11). Tracking them
# keeps every link in this repo resolvable and gives each teammate the
# playbook and working docs straight from a clone.
#
# Session chatter still stays out — notes, scratch files and one-off reports
# are not documents, and do not belong in the submission.
*_SESSION_NOTES.md
scratch/

# ---- Source artwork ----
# The full-size renders the UI images were derived from. Kept on disk so the
# WebP set can be regenerated at another size, but never committed: they are
# ~3 MB of originals whose 260 KB processed output is what the app actually
# ships (frontend/public/img/). Root-anchored so it cannot swallow a .jpg that
# genuinely belongs to the app.
/*.jpg
